vendor_popup_5=This password opens the secret room behind the portrait of Havelock Sweeting.
vendor_popup_6=This password opens the secret room behind the portrait of Mopsus.
vendor_popup_7=This password opens the secret room behind the portrait of Bertie Bott.
vendor_popup_8=This password opens the secret room behind the portrait of Derwent Shimpling.
vendor_popup_9=This password opens the secret room behind the portrait of Tilly Toke.
WizardDesc_1=Dorcas Wellbeloved (1812-1904). Founder of the Society for Distressed Witches.
WizardDesc_100=Ethelred the Ever-Ready (Middle Ages). Famous for taking offence and cursing complete strangers. Killed in a duel.
WizardDesc_101=Albus Dumbledore. Headmaster of Hogwarts.
WizardDesc_102=Lady Carmilla Sanguina (1561-1757). Bathed in the blood of her victims to keep her youth and beauty.
WizardDesc_103=Amarillo Lestoat (1776-1977). Famous American vampire. Author of "Soliloquies of the Undead", written so that a bored reader falls into a stupor and becomes easy prey.
WizardDesc_104=Sir Herbert Varney (1858-1889). A Victorian vampire who did not last long (by the standards of the undead). Preyed on the women of London in the 1880s and was destroyed by a special squad of the Department for the Regulation and Control of Magical Creatures.
WizardDesc_105=Blodwyn Bludd (1923-?). Known as the "Vampire of the Valleys". Famous for his fine baritone and his habit of singing to his victims before biting them.
WizardDesc_106=Count Vlad Drakul (1390-?). The famous vampire who inspired Bram Stoker's Count Dracula. Father of Vlad the Impaler.
WizardDesc_107=Eargit the Ugly. Spoke for the goblins at the Wizards' Council in the 14th century.
WizardDesc_108=Alguff the Awful. A smelly, quarrelsome goblin. Once tried to sell bottles of his own sweat to a Dungbomb factory.
WizardDesc_109=Ug the Unreliable. A notorious goblin swindler. Organised races of invisible horses, then ran off with all the takings.
WizardDesc_110=Urg the Unclean. Led several goblin rebellions in the 18th century.
WizardDesc_111=Gringott. Founder of Gringotts Wizarding Bank.
WizardDesc_112=Baba Yaga (Middle Ages). Russian witch. Lived in a hut on chicken legs. Ate small children for breakfast (and possibly for lunch and dinner too).
WizardDesc_113=Malodora Grymm (Middle Ages). Hid her true looks with a beautifying potion and married a king, keeping up the disguise with an enchanted mirror. Out of envy she fed the fairest girl in the land a poisoned apple.
WizardDesc_114=Letitia Somnolens (Middle Ages). A witch who, envying the king's daughter, made her prick her finger on a spindle soaked in the Draught of Living Death. A young wizard put Wiggenweld Potion on his lips, kissed the princess and woke her from the trance.
WizardDesc_115=Mother Hubbard (Middle Ages). Lured stray animals into her home and starved them to death.
WizardDesc_116=Cordelia Misericordia (1298-1401). Spoke for the witches at the Wizards' Council in the 14th century.
WizardDesc_117=Bran the Bloodthirsty (Middle Ages). Lived in a castle at the top of an enchanted beanstalk. Apparently liked bread made of ground bones, washed down with the blood of Englishmen. Killed by a boy called Jack.
WizardDesc_118=Cyclops (Ancient Greece). A one-eyed giant who lived in a cave at the foot of Mount Etna. Killed by the Greek hero Odysseus.
WizardDesc_119=Goliath (Biblical times). A giant mercenary who fought for the Philistines against the Israelites. Killed by a young man with a sling.
WizardDesc_120=Morholt (early Middle Ages). A giant, brother of the King of Ireland. Defending his life, he wounded the Celtic hero Tristan with a poisoned sword.
WizardDesc_121=Hengist of Upper Barnton (15th century). A giant. Killed by the famous giant-slayer Gifford Ollerton.
WizardDesc_122=Common Welsh Green dragon. The least dangerous of all dragons. When calm it avoids people. Breathes fire in thin jets.
WizardDesc_123=Hebridean Black dragon. Another native British breed, more aggressive than its Welsh cousin. Feeds mostly on deer; a few attacks on large dogs have been recorded.
WizardDesc_124=Hungarian Horntail dragon. Thought to be the most dangerous breed of all. Can breathe a tongue of flame up to fifty feet long.
WizardDesc_125=Romanian Longhorn dragon. Its horns go into many potions and are highly prized, so its numbers have fallen sharply in recent years.
WizardDesc_126=Norwegian Ridgeback dragon. Now the rarest breed of dragon. Attacks nearly any large land mammal.
WizardDesc_127=Imp. Found only in Britain and Ireland. Has a crude sense of humour: it loves to push and trip up anyone not paying attention.
WizardDesc_128=Doxy. Often mistaken for a fairy. Lives in bushes and attacks anyone who comes too close. Its teeth are sharp and venomous.
WizardDesc_129=Bowtruckle. A tree guardian, cleverly hidden by all sorts of charms. May try to gouge out the eyes of anyone who comes near its tree looking threatening.
WizardDesc_13=Dymphna Furmage (1612-1698). Once carried off by Cornish pixies, she lived in terror of them ever after. Famous for her many fruitless attempts to make the Ministry of Magic wipe out all pixies.
WizardDesc_130=Billywig. The sting of this insect's long, thin sting makes you giddy and then makes you float. Dried Billywig stings go into several potions.
WizardDesc_131=Gnome. A common garden pest. Gnomes hide in holes and pop out to trip up passers-by. To get one out of a garden, swing it round well and throw it over the fence.
WizardDesc_132=Giant Squid. The bane of ancient sailors, and of Hogwarts students who take it into their heads to dive in the lake.
WizardDesc_133=Manticore. A rare and dangerous beast. Croons softly as it devours its prey. Its sting kills instantly.
WizardDesc_134=Unicorn. Very shy; usually avoids people, and would rather let a witch come near than a wizard. Spellcasting can frighten it. Unicorn blood has precious magical properties.
WizardDesc_135=Mountain Troll. Common in mountainous country. Very strong but stupid. Tries to club anyone who goes past.
WizardDesc_136=Phoenix. A noble creature that lives practically for ever, as it can rise again from its ashes. Its song is magical and its tears have healing powers.
wizarddesc_137=Two-headed newt. Swims a lot and loves pondweed. You can buy one at the Magical Menagerie in Diagon Alley.
wizarddesc_138=Giant purple toad. Eats dead flies and other insects. Has a long green tongue.
wizarddesc_139=Gytrash. A spirit that looks like a large dog. Gytrashes are found alone and in packs in the Forbidden Forest.
wizarddesc_140=Kelpie. Lives in streams and rivers. Kneels to invite passers-by to ride on its back, then drags its riders under the water and tries to eat them.
wizarddesc_141=Streeler. A big orange snail with a venomous shell. Handle only with protective gloves.
wizarddesc_142=Zou Yen (4th century BC). Chinese alchemist.
wizarddesc_143=Falco Aesalon (Ancient Greece). The first recorded Animagus. Could turn into a falcon.
wizarddesc_144=Professor Armando Dippet. A former Headmaster of Hogwarts. Died in 1940.
WizardDesc_18=Charlotte Pinkstone, born 1922. A famous witch who campaigns to repeal the Statute of Secrecy and tell Muggles that wizards exist. Has been charged several times with breaking the Statute.
WizardDesc_2=Thaddeus Thurkell (1632-1692). A wizard whose seven sons were all completely without magic. In despair he turned them all into hedgehogs.
WizardDesc_24=Mirabella Plunkett (1839-?). On holiday at Loch Lomond she fell in love with a merman. When her parents forbade the marriage she turned herself into a cod and was never seen again.
WizardDesc_26=Wendelin the Weird (dates unknown). Enjoyed being burned at the stake so much that she let herself be caught forty-seven times in various disguises.
WizardDesc_32=Bowman Wright (1492-1560). Inventor of the Golden Snitch.
WizardDesc_33=Joscelind Wadcock (born 1911). Chaser for the Puddlemere United Quidditch team. Holds the record for the most goals in a single match (Puddlemere v Norfolk Bats, 1931).
WizardDesc_39=Harry Potter. The Boy Who Lived.
WizardDesc_42=Elfrida Clagg (1612-1687). Chief of the Wizards' Council.
WizardDesc_43=Grogan Stump (1770-1884). A famous Minister for Magic, in office from 1811.
WizardDesc_45=Glanmore Peakes (1677-1761). Slayer of the Sea Serpent of Cromer.
WizardDesc_46=Hesper Starkey (1881-1973). A witch who studied how the phases of the moon affect potions.
WizardDesc_48=Gunhilda of Gorsemoor (1556-1639). A one-eyed, hump-backed witch who discovered a cure for Dragon Pox.
WizardDesc_49=Godric Gryffindor (Middle Ages). One of the founders of Hogwarts. Gryffindor House bears his name.
WizardDesc_5=Sacharissa Tugwood (1874-1966). Pioneer of beauty magic. Invented a cure for spots made from Bubotuber pus.
WizardDesc_53=Fulbert the Fearful (1014-1097). Famous for his extraordinary cowardice. Never left his house, and died when it collapsed on him after a defensive charm went wrong.
WizardDesc_55=Cliodna (Middle Ages). An Irish druidess who discovered the magical properties of moon-dew.
WizardDesc_56=Morgan le Fay (Middle Ages). Half-sister of King Arthur. A dark sorceress and enemy of Merlin.
WizardDesc_59=Mungo Bonham (1560-1659). A famous healer. Founder of St Mungo's Hospital for Magical Maladies and Injuries.
WizardDesc_6=Wilfred Elphick (1112-1199). The first wizard to be killed by an African Erumpent.
WizardDesc_60=Gwenog Jones (born 1968). Captain and Beater of the only all-female Quidditch team in the world, the Holyhead Harpies.
WizardDesc_67=Helga Hufflepuff (Middle Ages). One of the founders of Hogwarts. Hufflepuff House bears her name.
WizardDesc_68=Jocunda Sykes (born 1915). The first to fly across the Atlantic on a broomstick.
WizardDesc_72=Norvel Twonk (1888-1957). Died saving a Muggle child from a Manticore that had escaped from a menagerie. Awarded the Order of Merlin, First Class, after his death.
WizardDesc_74=Oswald Beamish (1850-1932). The world's first champion of goblin rights.
WizardDesc_75=Beatrix Bloxam (1794-1810). Author of the "Toadstool Tales" books for children, later banned because they made children feel sick.
WizardDesc_77=Rowena Ravenclaw (Middle Ages). One of the founders of Hogwarts. One of the school's four houses bears her name.
WizardDesc_78=Roderick Plumpton (1889-1987). Seeker for the England Quidditch team. Holds the record for the fastest Snitch capture: three and a half seconds after the start of the game.
WizardDesc_81=Crispin Cronk (1795-1872). Sent to Azkaban for keeping sphinxes in his garden.
WizardDesc_82=Cyprian Youdle (1312-1357). The only Quidditch referee ever to die during a match. The curse was never traced, but it is thought to have come from a spectator.
WizardDesc_86=Edgar Stroulger (1703-1798). Inventor of the Sneakoscope.
WizardDesc_87=Salazar Slytherin (Middle Ages). One of the founders of Hogwarts. Slytherin House bears his name.
WizardDesc_92=Honoria Nutcombe (1665-1743). Founder of the Society for the Reformation of Hags.
WizardDesc_99=Ignatia Wildsmith (1227-1320). Inventor of Floo Powder.
